# Pinned to the SwiftFormat version below. Newer releases add default rules that
# flag the codebase's existing deliberate style (see the --disable entries).
# Revisit tracked in GitHub #196 — unpin, adopt current defaults, bulk-reformat once.
--minversion 0.62.1

# Rules opted out because they conflict with established style, and a whitespace-only
# reformat now would churn every open branch. wrapIfStatementBodies/wrapIfExpressionBodies
# are cosmetic (one-line `if x { return }` is fine here); preferForLoop is a
# forEach→for rewrite we don't want forced. wrapMultilineStatementBraces stays ON —
# it enforces the brace-on-own-line style the codebase already uses.
--disable wrapIfStatementBodies,wrapIfExpressionBodies,preferForLoop

--indent 4
--allman false
--semicolons never
--linebreaks lf
--trimwhitespace nonblank-lines
--importgrouping preserve
--wraparguments preserve
--wrapcollections preserve
--trailingcommas never
--strip-unused-args closure-only
--self remove
--maxwidth 140
--exclude .build,reminders-cli/.build,calendar-cli/.build,contacts-cli/.build,mail-cli/.build,text-cli/.build
